<!--Post: 58--><!--Time: 1085340053-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST58"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Wichitaboy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Wichitaboy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, May 23, 2004 - 12:20 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->1.&#41; Julie Otero &#40;DOD 01-15-74&#41; and Kathryn Bright &#40;DOD 04-04-74&#41; worked on the same assembly line at Coleman. <BR> <BR>2.&#41; Michael Williams the supervisor from the same assembly line at Coleman was shot 4 days prior to the Otero murders. <BR> <BR>3.&#41; Michael Williams’s father was head of personnel at Coleman. He worked in the Human Resources Department, which was located at New York and Central. &#40;Approximately 1500 E Central&#41; <BR> <BR>4.&#41; Sherry Baker a 23 year old WSU student was murdered 11-12-74 at 603 New York. This is one of the top three cold cases that are similar to BTK. <BR> <BR>5.&#41; 603 New York is only a block away from the Coleman Human Resources Department. <BR> <BR>6.&#41; The Coleman factory at 2nd and St Francis is only 2 blocks from where BTK made the telephone call notifying police about Nancy Fox.  The Coleman Human Resources Department is only 8 blocks away from the telephone. <BR> <BR>7.&#41; What do you think? <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 58-->
<!--Post: 59--><!--Time: 1085346407-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST59"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Doone<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Doone<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, May 23, 2004 - 2:06 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->DThe Otero and Bright murders occured only 3 months apart.  I had never realized they were so close together.  I know that Mrs Otero had been laid off prior to her murder.  It seems logical that they both worked at Coleman has to be more then a coincidence.  I assume Wichita Police checked this angle, but didn&#39;t find a connection.  It still seems probable BTK knew the Oteros, but from Kevin Bright I&#39;m sure we would have heard if his sister knew their attacker, so , who knows?  Kevin Bright is giving KAKE tv an interview and it&#39;ll air on Tuesdays 10 oclock news.  Maybe he&#39;ll have new information that has been withheld from the public.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 59-->
<!--Post: 310--><!--Time: 1087875097-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST310"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bookworm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bookworm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, June 21, 2004 - 8:31 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Maybe the human resources department should check their files for anyone with a gruge against the company. That&#39;s how they caught the Mad Bomber along with a profile.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 310-->
<!--Post: 319--><!--Time: 1087947370-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST319"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bookworm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bookworm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, June 22, 2004 - 4:36 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Since Julie Otero and Katherine Bright worked on the same &#34;line&#34; maybe their connection has something to do with the Transcontinental And Transport Company &#40;TAT&#41; also called the &#34;Lindbergh Line&#34;. March 17, St. Patrick&#39;s Day, and &#34;Lucky Lindy&#34;. New York to Los Angeles with a stop in Wichita. Otero had a son Charlie. Just a thought.  <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.kansasaviationmuseum.org/aerodrome/building.html" target=_top>http://www.kansasaviationmuseum.org/aerodrome/buil ding.html</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 319-->
<!--Post: 332--><!--Time: 1088114807-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST332"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Wichitaboy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Wichitaboy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, June 24, 2004 - 3:06 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I just found out that Kevin Bright worked at Coleman also.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 332-->
<!--Post: 361--><!--Time: 1088475836-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST361"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Midtown<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Midtown<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, June 28, 2004 - 7:23 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Does anyone know if the employees at Coleman wore uniforms at the time of the murders or prior to it?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 361-->
<!--Post: 364--><!--Time: 1088549178-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST364"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bookworm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bookworm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, June 29, 2004 - 3:46 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Was Mrs. Otero laid off anytime around Christmas? The initials of the family members that were killed are all JO. JO, JO, JO. In Spanish, that would be pronounced HO, HO, HO, HO. J sounds like H.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
